  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd the Waterjet Profile workflow before the Plasma workflow in the MCP guide.\nShow the machine file, nozzle definition, parameter keys, units and current post limits.\nState that the workflow requires the pending implementation in #1883 (PR #3058).\nRecord the documentation decision in its issue file.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe guide describes Plasma Profile but omits Waterjet Profile.\nAgents cannot find the waterjet tool calls or parameter keys.\n\n## Tests\n\nRead the parameter DTO and MCP workflow test at PR #3058 head aded58c477b18dd9c21b502be39dbf057dec0c4c.\nThe three new documentation pins are:\n\n- test_waterjet_workflow_documents_machine_and_nozzle\n- test_waterjet_workflow_documents_operation_parameters\n- test_waterjet_workflow_documents_availability_and_limits\n\nAll three fail on the unchanged upstream guide.\nAll three pass with the added section.\nThe mutation restores the guide from upstream/main: all three fail.\nRestore the fixed guide: all three pass.\nThe complete Python documentation suite passes all seven tests.\nCommand: `python3 -m unittest discover -s .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/tests -p test_*.py -v`.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes.\nThe gate selects zero Rust test steps because no crate changes.\nClippy does not apply because no Rust crate changes.\nAn initial gate run was void because staging changed the index; the stable rerun passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo live MCP session, machine, stock simulation or NC posting ran.\nThe runtime implementation and its MCP test are absent from upstream/main.\nThis change documents the pending contract; it adds no runtime support.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes the three paths in this change.\nPR #3058 supplies the runtime implementation in other files.\nThe guide states that dependency explicitly.\n\nEffort: low\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3048\n",
